{"id":"RI-local_preemption-1","technology":"solar;wind","policy_type":"local_preemption","who_decides":"state_board","state_body":"Energy Facility Siting Board","threshold_mw":"solar:40;wind:40","summary":"For major energy facilities the Siting Board is the licensing authority for every permit or variance that state law or local ordinance would require; local boards hear the matter but only send findings and a recommendation to the Siting Board.","statute_citation":"R.I. Gen. Laws § 42-98-7(a)(1), (2)","statute_url":"https://webserver.rilegislature.gov/Statutes/TITLE42/42-98/42-98-7.htm","evidence_level":"primary_source","verification":"verified","reviewed_on":"2026-10-09"},
{"id":"RI-other-1","technology":"solar;wind","policy_type":"other","who_decides":null,"state_body":null,"threshold_mw":null,"summary":"Distributed generation projects in core forests (unbroken forest blocks of 250 acres or more) cannot take part in the Renewable Energy Growth program, and net-metering systems must be sited outside core forests, unless they are on a preferred site such as a landfill, brownfield, parking lot or rooftop (net metering also exempts projects already in the permit or interconnection process on April 15, 2023); on preferred sites in a core forest no more than 100,000 square feet of core forest may be cleared, and new net-metering projects cannot be split across adjoining core-forest parcels except on preferred sites.","statute_citation":"R.I. Gen. Laws sections 39-26.6-3(6), (7), (15); 39-26.4-2(2), (19); 39-26.4-3(a)(1)(ii), (iii)","statute_url":"https://webserver.rilegislature.gov/Statutes/TITLE39/39-26.6/39-26.6-3.htm","evidence_level":"primary_source","verification":"verified","reviewed_on":"2026-10-09"},
{"id":"RI-siting_authority-1","technology":"solar;wind","policy_type":"siting_authority","who_decides":"hybrid","state_body":"Energy Facility Siting Board","threshold_mw":"solar:40;wind:40","summary":"Generating facilities of 40 MW or more are major energy facilities licensed by the Energy Facility Siting Board; smaller facilities are regulated by city and town zoning.","statute_citation":"R.I. Gen. Laws §§ 42-98-3(e), 42-98-7(a)","statute_url":"https://webserver.rilegislature.gov/Statutes/TITLE42/42-98/42-98-3.htm","evidence_level":"primary_source","verification":"verified","reviewed_on":"2026-10-09"}
